From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:30:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Leave SdMmcPciGliDxe out of the payload

SdMmcPciGliDxe drives the SDHCI controllers of Genesys Logic (GL9750,
GL9755, GL9763E: PCI vendor 0x17a0, the only one it binds). No board of
ouroBIOS has one: the card reader of the W541 is an O2 Micro OZ777, which
SdMmcPciHcDxe of MdeModulePkg drives, and the M920x has no reader. The
driver was 4,700 lines of the volume, dispatched at every boot to bind
nothing.

The module and its two lines of the platform go. SdMmcPciHcDxe, EmmcDxe
and SdDxe stay as they are.
